<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Delivery gate for the same-millisecond trade drop
       (docs/trade-store-same-millisecond-drop-2026-08-11.md §6 item 3).

       ONE question: does Deribit's trades.BTC-PERPETUAL.100ms channel actually DELIVER
       several trades sharing a millisecond timestamp? If it does, TradeStoreWriter.vb:149's
       `<=` guard is discarding them and a guard fix is the answer. If it does not, the
       trades never arrived and a guard fix would change nothing — the capture strategy
       itself would need rethinking.

       DELIBERATELY STANDALONE. It links NOTHING from the app: no Core files, no settings
       loader, no TradeStoreWriter. It cannot read or write any file the collector uses, so
       it can be run on the same box as a live collector without touching its state.

       Read-only against the venue: one public WS connection, public channels, no auth,
       no orders. net8.0 + zero WinForms — runs on Linux via `dotnet WsTradeProbe.dll`. -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>DeribitVerdictEngine</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>WsTradeProbe</AssemblyName>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <StartupObject>DeribitVerdictEngine.WsTradeProbeProgram</StartupObject>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
